From 940ee1c34f85549e9c1e3b65da4b32abd06002a6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: kebab bring-up <local@invalid>
Date: Fri, 18 Sep 2026 12:29:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] kebab: pin cam_vdig (pm8008_l1) to 1.104V, the nearest
 settable step to vendor 1.1V

The vendor devicetree specifies cam_vdig as a single point, not a range:

  kebab-19805-camera.dts, qcom,cam-sensor@2:
    rgltr-min-voltage / rgltr-max-voltage = 0x10c8e0 = 1100000uV

Declared here as a 528000-1200000 range, the core parks L1P at the range
maximum, so it has been running at 1.2V -- 100mV over vendor spec.

1100000uV cannot be requested literally. The pm8008 LDO steps in 8mV, so
the regulator core rounds the minimum up to 1104000 and the maximum down
to 1096000, producing an inverted window and refusing the constraint:

  pm8008_l1: unsupportable voltage constraints 1104000-1096000uV
  qcom-pm8008-regulator: failed to register regulator ldo1: -22
  qcom-pm8008-regulator: probe ... failed with error -22

Because ldo1 registration failing aborts the driver's whole probe, none
of L1-L7 get registered -- so this takes out cam_vio (L4, 1.8V) as well
as cam_vdig. With both rails gone every device on the camera bus is
unpowered, the CCI controller cannot even complete an address phase, and
the entire bus reports "master 0 queue 1 timeout" rather than a NACK.
The module EEPROM at 0x50/0x58, which had ACKed reliably until now,
goes silent too. That is a pure self-inflicted power failure and says
nothing whatsoever about the image sensor.

This also retroactively explains patch 0066. 0066 made this identical
mistake, and 0068 reverted it on the strength of the failure changing
from -ENXIO to -ETIMEDOUT, recording that as a sensor-level regression.
It was not: it was this same PMIC probe cascade. The 1.1V rail value has
therefore still never actually been evaluated.

Use 1104000uV, the nearest settable step above the vendor's nominal
(1096000 is the nearest below; both are within 0.4% of 1.1V).
---
 .../boot/dts/qcom/sm8250-oneplus-kebab.dts    | 35 +++++++++++++++----
 1 file changed, 29 insertions(+), 6 deletions(-)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8250-oneplus-kebab.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8250-oneplus-kebab.dts
index 8a76fd93e..3b9b78fcb 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8250-oneplus-kebab.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8250-oneplus-kebab.dts
@@ -1894,12 +1894,35 @@ pm8008: pmic@8 {
 		regulators {
 			L1P: ldo1 {
 				regulator-name = "pm8008_l1";
-				/* kebab-19805-camera.dts's cam-sensor@2 rgltr-min/max-voltage
-				 * for cam_vdig are both 0x10c8e0 = 1100000uV exactly -- not a
-				 * range. Pin it instead of leaving it to float to this
-				 * range's max (1.2V), which was 100mV over vendor spec. */
-				regulator-min-microvolt = <528000>;
-				regulator-max-microvolt = <1200000>;
+				/* cam_vdig. kebab-19805-camera.dts's cam-sensor@2 gives
+				 * rgltr-min-voltage == rgltr-max-voltage == 0x10c8e0 ==
+				 * 1100000uV for this rail -- a single point, not a range.
+				 * Left as a 528000-1200000 range the core parks it at the
+				 * range max, i.e. 1.2V, which is 100mV over vendor spec and
+				 * was confirmed live in regulator_summary.
+				 *
+				 * Patch 0066 already tried pinning this to 1.1V and was
+				 * reverted by 0068 as a "regression" because the failure
+				 * changed from -ENXIO to -ETIMEDOUT. That verdict is not
+				 * usable: 0066 ran while VANA was still inverted by patch
+				 * 0060, so the sensor's analog rail was switched OFF for the
+				 * whole transaction. Both outcomes were measured on an
+				 * unpowered sensor and neither means anything. 0077 fixed
+				 * the polarity, so retry the vendor value on its merits.
+				 *
+				 * NB: 1100000 itself is NOT settable on this PMIC. The
+				 * pm8008 LDO steps in 8mV, so the core rounds min up to
+				 * 1104000 and max down to 1096000, ends up with min > max
+				 * and bails:
+				 *   pm8008_l1: unsupportable voltage constraints
+				 *              1104000-1096000uV
+				 *   qcom-pm8008-regulator: failed to register ldo1: -22
+				 * That kills the whole pm8008-regulator probe, so L1 AND L4
+				 * (cam_vdig AND cam_vio) both vanish and every device on the
+				 * camera bus loses power -- the EEPROM included. Use the
+				 * nearest representable step instead. */
+				regulator-min-microvolt = <1104000>;
+				regulator-max-microvolt = <1104000>;
 				/* cam_vdig for the front sensor (1.1V, per
 				 * kebab-19805-camera.dts's cam-sensor@2). imx471.c
 				 * only regulator_bulk_gets "vana" itself, so keep
-- 
